---
/**
 * LegalContent — the shared body for each legal page.
 * Renders different content based on the `page` prop. English only (per PRD).
 */
import { site } from '~/config/site';

interface Props {
  page: 'about' | 'privacy-policy' | 'terms-of-service' | 'copyright' | 'contact';
}
const { page } = Astro.props;
const game = site.game.name;
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

{
  page === 'about' && (
    <>
      <p>
        {site.name} is an independent fan-made field manual for {game}, a {site.game.genre} on{' '}
        {site.game.platform} developed by {site.game.developer}. The site focuses on the decisions a
        commander makes before and during an outbreak: where to hold, how to move civilians, which
        forces to deploy, and what to check when a plan fails.
      </p>
      <h2>What We Cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Beginner planning and the prepare-then-outbreak loop</li>
        <li>Evacuation corridors, safe zones, gates, and civilian protection</li>
        <li>Ground-force roles, air support, defensive structures, and upgrades</li>
        <li>Boston and Miami player case studies with timestamped sources</li>
        <li>Co-op, custom maps, system requirements, and frequently asked questions</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How We Research</h2>
      <p>
        We start with the official {game} Steam page, the developer's press kit, and Steam Workshop
        listings. Where a guide relies on a player video or a third-party report, we identify the
        source and include a timestamp or link when one is available. We distinguish official facts,
        player-reported results, and our own planning advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not claim to have independently tested every mechanic. {game} is in Early Access, so
        unit values, interface labels, and balance can change between builds. Each guide shows when
        it was last reviewed.
      </p>
      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is not affiliated with or endorsed by {site.game.developer}. Game names,
        screenshots, and other game assets belong to their respective rights holders and are used
        for identification, commentary, and player guidance.
      </p>
      <h2>Corrections and Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Found an error, an outdated mechanic, or a source we should add? Open an issue in the{' '}
        <a href={site.contactUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          public corrections tracker
        </a>
        . No account is needed to read the site; a GitHub account is needed to post.
      </p>
    </>
  )
}

{
  page === 'privacy-policy' && (
    <>
      <p>
        This privacy policy describes how {site.name} ("we", "us", or "our") handles information
        when you visit this website.
      </p>
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is a static fan-made website. There are no user accounts, comments, newsletters,
        or checkout flows. We do not ask visitors to submit personal information. Analytics is loaded
        only after you accept the cookie prompt, and no third-party display advertising is currently
        enabled.
      </p>
      <h2>Information Processed by Service Providers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site and processes request data such as IP address,
          requested URL, user agent, and approximate location for content delivery, security, and
          abuse prevention.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Tag Manager</strong> (container <code>GTM-N752K4GB</code>) loads only after
          you press <em>Accept</em> in the cookie banner. The container is used to manage measurement
          tags, which may include Google Analytics 4. Those tags may set cookies and collect page
          views, approximate location, device and browser information, and interaction events.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local browser storage</strong> holds your cookie choice
          (<code>aw-cookie-consent</code>) and theme preference (<code>theme</code>). This stays in
          your browser and is not sent to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>External links</strong> to Steam, YouTube, GitHub, and other sites open only when
          you choose them. Those services apply their own privacy policies and may set cookies after
          you arrive.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Cookies and Consent</h2>
      <p>
        Before you accept, the Google Tag Manager container is not loaded. If you decline, it stays
        off for that choice stored in your browser. You can clear site data in your browser at any
        time; the banner will appear again on your next visit. Google Analytics cookies can also be
        controlled through your browser settings and Google's available opt-out controls.
      </p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        No third-party display advertising is currently enabled on this site. If advertising is
        added later, this policy will be updated before ads are served, including the relevant
        partners, cookie use, and opt-out choices.
      </p>
      <h2>Data Sharing and Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information. Service providers process data under their own terms
        and retention schedules. Because this site has no accounts or user database, we generally do
        not hold personal data that we can retrieve or delete on your behalf.
      </p>
      <h2>Your Choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can decline analytics, clear cookies and local storage, or use browser privacy controls.
        For a privacy question about this site, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> or open an issue in the{' '}
        <a href={site.contactUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          public corrections tracker
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
        information from children.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page.</p>
    </>
  )
}

{
  page === 'terms-of-service' && (
    <>
      <p>By accessing {site.name}, you agree to the following terms of service.</p>
      <h2>Use of Content</h2>
      <p>
        All guides, articles, and reference material on this site are provided for personal,
        non-commercial use. You may not copy, republish, or redistribute our content without
        attribution and a link back to the original page.
      </p>
      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        We strive for accuracy but make no warranties regarding the completeness or correctness of
        any content. {game} is frequently updated, and information may become outdated. Always
        verify critical information in-game.
      </p>
      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to external websites (official game channels, video tutorials, etc.) that we
        do not control. We are not responsible for the content or practices of third-party sites.
      </p>
      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        {game} and all related trademarks, logos, and assets are the property of{' '}
        {site.game.developer}. {site.name} is an independent fan project and is not affiliated with
        or endorsed by {site.game.developer}.
      </p>
      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Use of this site is at your own risk. We are not liable for any damages arising from your
        use of the site or reliance on its content.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise these terms at any time. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes
        acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>
    </>
  )
}

{
  page === 'copyright' && (
    <>
      <h2>Copyright Notice</h2>
      <p>
        © {year} {site.name}. All original articles, guides, and written content on this site are
        the intellectual property of {site.name} and its contributors.
      </p>
      <h2>Game Assets</h2>
      <p>
        {game}, including its name, logo, characters, artwork, and other related assets, is the
        property of {site.game.developer}. All {game} content is used on this wiki under fair use
        for the purpose of providing informational guides to players. {site.name} claims no
        ownership of any {game} intellectual property.
      </p>
      <h2>DMCA / Takedown</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe any content on this site infringes your copyright, open an issue in the{' '}
        <a href={site.contactUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          public corrections tracker
        </a>{' '}
        with the page URL, the work you believe is infringed, and enough information for us to
        review the request. We will respond to valid requests promptly.
      </p>
      <h2>Fan-Made Notice</h2>
      <p>{site.legalNotice}</p>
    </>
  )
}

{
  page === 'contact' && (
    <>
      {/* h2, not h1 — LegalPage already renders the page H1 (single-H1 rule). */}
      <h2>Contact {site.name}</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is an independent fan-made wiki. Use the public corrections tracker for content
        errors, outdated mechanics, source suggestions, or copyright concerns. No account is needed
        to read the site; a GitHub account is needed to open an issue.
      </p>
      <h2>Site Corrections</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Report an issue:</strong>{' '}
          <a href={site.contactUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {site.contactUrl}
          </a>
        </li>
        {site.social.github && (
          <li>
            <strong>Project repository:</strong>{' '}
            <a href={site.social.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              {site.social.github}
            </a>
          </li>
        )}
        {site.contactEmail && (
          <li>
            <strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>
          </li>
        )}
        {site.social.official && (
          <li>
            <strong>Game's official Steam page:</strong>{' '}
            <a href={site.social.official} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              {site.social.official}
            </a>
          </li>
        )}
      </ul>
      <h2>What to Include</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The page URL and the section that needs correction</li>
        <li>What is wrong or out of date</li>
        <li>A source, screenshot, or date/version where possible</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Contributing</h2>
      <p>
        The site is built from a public repository. Source corrections and additional evidence can
        be proposed through the corrections tracker or a pull request.
      </p>
      <h2>Reporting Issues</h2>
      <p>
        For copyright or takedown requests, see our{' '}
        <a href="/copyright/">Copyright page</a>.
      </p>
    </>
  )
}
